## 1. Introduction and Purpose

This comprehensive Leave and Attendance Policy establishes guidelines for all employees regarding leave entitlements, attendance expectations, timekeeping, and absence management. The policy is designed to:

- Ensure fair and consistent treatment of all employees
- Maintain operational continuity and business performance
- Comply with applicable Indian labor laws and regulations
- Provide clarity on employee rights and manager responsibilities
- Support employee well-being through adequate rest and leave provisions

This policy applies to all full-time regular employees, probationary employees, and fixed-term contract employees of BrightPath Analytics. Interns may have different entitlements as specified in their offer letters.

---

## 2. Attendance and Timekeeping

### 2.1 Standard Working Hours

**Full-Time Employees:**
- Working hours: Monday to Friday, 9:30 a.m. to 6:30 p.m. IST
- Total hours per week: 40 hours
- Lunch break: 1 hour unpaid (typically 12:30 p.m. to 2:00 p.m., at employee discretion within team coordination)
- No work is expected on Saturday, Sunday, or declared public holidays

**Flexibility:**
- Some teams or roles may have adjusted start/end times (e.g., 9:00 a.m.–5:30 p.m. or 10:00 a.m.–7:00 p.m.) to accommodate customer needs or time zones
- Any adjusted hours must be approved by the manager and documented in the HRIS system
- Once adjusted hours are approved, the employee is expected to adhere to the new schedule consistently

### 2.2 Attendance Recording

All employees must record their attendance using the HRIS mobile app or web portal:

**Check-In:**
- Employee checks in upon arrival at the office or at 9:30 a.m. when working from home
- Check-in by 9:45 a.m. is recommended; check-ins after 9:45 a.m. are recorded as late
- Remote employees must check in at the start of their working day

**Check-Out:**
- Employee checks out upon departure from office or at the end of working day (6:30 p.m.) when working from home
- System records actual check-out time; flexibility is allowed for occasional 5–10 minute variations
- Employees working overtime should note this in a comment when checking out

**Monitoring:**
- Attendance records are reviewed by managers weekly
- Automated alerts notify managers if an employee doesn't check in by 9:50 a.m.
- Summary attendance reports are reviewed monthly during 1:1 meetings

**System Access:**
- HRIS portal is accessible 24/7 for checking in/out
- Mobile app allows check-in from any location (office, work-from-home setup, or on the road)
- Technical issues (app crashes, system downtime) should be reported to IT immediately; manual entries can be approved by HR

### 2.3 Late Arrivals and Early Departures

**Late Arrivals (after 9:45 a.m.):**
- Occasional late arrivals (1–2 times per month) due to traffic, personal emergencies, or unexpected situations are understood and do not require formal documentation
- Frequent late arrivals (3+ times per month) will be addressed by the manager in 1:1s
- Repeated late arrivals may result in:
  - First reminder: Informal manager conversation
  - Second occurrence: Written reminder or verbal warning
  - Third occurrence: Formal written warning and potential performance counseling

**Persistent Lateness (Pattern Over 1 Month):**
- If an employee is late more than 3 times in a month, the manager will have a formal conversation to understand the issue (e.g., family situation, health issue, commute problem)
- Solutions might include adjusted start time, work-from-home option, or performance improvement plan

**Early Departures (before 6:30 p.m.):**
- Occasional early departures with manager approval are acceptable (e.g., medical appointment, important personal matter)
- Employee should notify the manager before leaving
- Early departure time should be recorded in the HRIS system

### 2.4 Attendance During Work-From-Home Days

Employees working from home on designated days or with remote work approval are expected to:
- Check in and out via the HRIS system at their regular working hours
- Be available and responsive during standard working hours (9:30 a.m.–6:30 p.m. IST)
- Respond to Slack, email, and calls within normal response times (typically within 30 minutes to 1 hour)
- Attend virtual meetings on time and with camera/audio as required
- Inform the manager if they need to step away for extended periods (e.g., doctor's appointment during work hours)

