## 12. Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: What if I fall sick while on approved annual leave?**  
A: If you become ill during approved leave and have medical proof, the days can be reclassified as sick leave. You should notify the manager with medical documentation. The annual leave days are returned to your balance.

**Q: Can I request leave for just 1–2 hours?**  
A: Typically, leave is recorded in half-day (4 hours) or full-day (8 hours) increments. Hourly leave is not the standard, but can be requested with manager approval for exceptional situations.

**Q: What if my manager denies my leave request without a good reason?**  
A: If you believe your leave request has been unfairly denied, you can escalate to your manager's manager or HR. Provide context about the request and the denial.

**Q: Do I lose my annual leave balance at year-end?**  
A: Any annual leave beyond 5 days that you don't carry over is forfeited at year-end. It is important to plan your leave and take it during the year.

**Q: Can I take leave while on a Performance Improvement Plan?**  
A: While on a PIP, leave is still available, but you should discuss with your manager. Critical leave periods may be restricted to allow focus on improvement goals.

**Q: What happens if I take sick leave immediately after annual leave?**  
A: If you take sick leave right after annual leave and there is a pattern, the manager may request medical certification to verify. Legitimate illness is covered; patterns that suggest misuse will be addressed.

